    "city": "mogadishu",
    "climate": "tropical-maritime",
    "vernacular": "Hot, dry-humid Indian Ocean coast city. The old districts (Hamar Weyne, Shangani) are tight lanes of 2-4 storey whitewashed coral-stone and limestone houses with flat roofs, carved doors and arched openings; the Italian-era core adds cream stucco Art Deco and classical public buildings with clay-tile roofs; modern Mogadishu is 2-6 storey concrete-frame blocks (many rebuilt after the civil war, some Turkish-built) in painted render with metal-sheet roofs, shopfronts and rooftop water tanks, often war-scarred; compounds are walled; sand ground, palms and neem.",
    "wallColours": [
      "#f1ece0",
      "#e1c68f",
