    "ground": "sand",
    "vegetation": [
      "palm",
      "acacia",
      "broadleaf"
    ],
    "ornament": "Banadiri arched doorways and carved wooden doors, coral-stone fretwork and lime plaster; mosque minarets (square or cylindrical) with domed mihrab (13th-century Fakr ad-Din type); Italian Art Deco fins, rounded corners and arcades on colonial buildings; bright painted shopfront signage; perimeter walls with razor wire in the modern city.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Architecture_of_Somalia",
        "what": "coral stone, sun-dried brick and limestone after Islam; Fakr ad-Din mosque 13th c. with marble and coral stone and domed mihrab; Italian-era classical buildings including Villa Somalia and Governor's Palace; later modernist buildings in chrome, steel and glass"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa_Somalia",
        "what": "originally a large squarish Art Deco building with stucco walls and tiled roof on high ground, inaugurated 1936; renovated and reopened 2025"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mogadishu_Cathedral",
        "what": "Norman/Gothic Revival Cefalu-based cathedral, 1923-28, twin 37.5 m towers; ruined"
      }
    ]
  },
